<title>BELGIUM: KB-Securities top Belgian broker in volume terms.</title>
<headline>KB-Securities top Belgian broker in volume terms.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>KB-Securities, a unit of Kredietbank, is the largest Belgian brokerage house in terms of volumes traded in 1996, an internal Brussels bourse document showed.</p>
<p>The brokerage confirmed its ranking. &quot;We are the biggest in volume terms,&quot; a KB Securities official told Reuters.</p>
<p>Numbers two and three are, respectively, Petercam SA and Dewaay, Servais &amp; Cie.</p>
<p>The other top-ten brokers -- in alphabetical order -- are:</p>
<p>Degroof Securities;</p>
<p>G-Securities ;</p>
<p>Mignon, Hanart, Declerck;</p>
<p>Nedee &amp; Co;</p>
<p>Puilaetco;</p>
<p>Smeets, Verbaet &amp; Co;</p>
<p>Vermeulen, Raemdonck.</p>
<p>-- Geert De Clercq, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6813, Fax +32 2 230 771</p>
